#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""deploy-packages: build goblin-skiff on naamah (amd64), graviton5 (arm64),
loongson (Kylin loongarch64) and this Mac, then publish the packages to
https://apt.goblinreactor.com/ and https://brew.goblinreactor.com/.

    ./deploy-packages plan                  show what would be built where
    ./deploy-packages                       source snapshot, all builds, publish
    ./deploy-packages source                only make the source snapshot
    ./deploy-packages build [--host H]      build (or retry) targets
    ./deploy-packages publish [--check]     publish a complete stage

The release source is a snapshot of the committed tree, and the upstream
GitHub repository must be public. Artifacts are staged in
~/goblin-deploy/<name>/<version>/. Publishing goes through hail (signing
key, reprepro, Homebrew tap, signed catalogs), then the changed files are
uploaded to the Cloudflare R2 buckets that serve both sites. Published
files are immutable: bump the version in the repository for a new release.

Only the PROJECT block differs between repositories; the shared driver
below it is identical everywhere.
"""

